{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/mutants.log; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md'","aggregated_output":"control  [push ids left open]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.04s\nmutant   [push ids left open]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.07s\ncontrol  [lists parsed from the text, not the rows]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.06s\nmutant   [lists parsed from the text, not the rows]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.09s\ncontrol  [the v12 check reads the text, not the lists]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.06s\nmutant   [the v12 check reads the text, not the lists]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.09s\ncontrol  [maxItems dropped for an empty list]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.04s\nmutant   [maxItems dropped for an empty list]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.07s\ncontrol  [the validator ignores maxItems]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.04s\nmutant   [the validator ignores maxItems]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.07s\ncontrol  [strict dropped from the outgoing format]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.06s\nmutant   [strict dropped from the outgoing format]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.09s\ncontrol  [the round sends the open format]: exit 0 2 passed, 5 deselected in 0.09s\nmutant   [the round sends the open format]: exit 1 CAUGHT 2 failed, 5 deselected in 0.12s\ncontrol  [the retry sends the open format]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.06s\nmutant   [the retry sends the open format]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.09s\ncontrol  [preflight checks judge rows against the fixed schema]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.05s\nmutant   [preflight checks judge rows against the fixed schema]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.08s\ncontrol  [preflight skips a malformed judge row before checking its format]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.05s\nmutant   [preflight skips a malformed judge row before checking its format]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.08s\ncontrol  [preflight does not fail on a missing judge format]: exit 0 1 passed, 6 deselected in 0.07s\nmutant   [preflight does not fail on a missing judge format]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 6 deselected in 0.08s\ncontrol  [the closed format drifts]: exit 0 1 passed, 3 deselected in 0.02s\nmutant   [the closed format drifts]: exit 1 CAUGHT 1 failed, 3 deselected in 0.05s\nexit 0\n     1\t# Citation-only judge version: build and $0 test result (D714)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Verdict:** judging-v12 and poc-v121 are built, and every registered $0 check passes (DESIGN.md §5, registered before the runs;\n     4\tD713). No paid call was made. Provider acceptance of the format, and whether the judge then picks the intended source, remain for\n     5\ta paid step that is Alex's to open (D712).\n     6\t\n     7\t## What was built (uncommitted)\n     8\t\n     9\t| File | Change |\n    10\t|---|---|\n    11\t| `src/hivemind/views/judging.py` | `judging-v12` added to `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS`, plus `CLOSED_LISTS` |\n    12\t| | `schema_for(version, lists)` closes the four id fields for v12: one shared `$defs` evidence enum, plain dependency and theme enums, `maxItems: 0` when a list is empty |\n    13\t| | `request_parts` returns the texts and the lists from the same rows; `build_prompt` delegates to it |\n    14\t| | `check_answer(..., lists)` checks membership against the lists under v12 |\n    15\t| | `round_of_judgements` sends each v12 view its own format, the retry included; v7/v8 still go through `build_prompt` with the frozen format |\n    16\t| `src/hivemind/model.py` | `check_schema` enforces `maxItems` |\n    17\t| `src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v12.txt` | a byte copy of judging-v7 (sha `d499c4b8…`) |\n    18\t| `poc/config/poc-v121.json` | poc-v118 with `rejudging.prompt_version` = judging-v12 |\n    19\t| `scripts/preflight.py` | part A checks judge rows against their saved format; a judge row without one, a malformed one included (Codex r39), fails `main` with exit 1 |\n    20\t| `tests/test_citation_lists.py` | 7 tests: T1c, T3, T3b, T5 (part A, and `main`'s exit) and the format-error path |\n    21\t| `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py` | 1 new test: the v12 prompt and two v12 formats pinned; the v7/v8 format sha unchanged |\n    22\t| `tests/test_live_lock.py` | part A's stub returns the new pair |\n    23\t\n    24\t**Checks of the build**\n    25\t- Suite: 388 passed, rerun after the preflight fix.\n    26\t- Mutants: 12 of 12 caught, each by its own assertion (`mutants.log`). The failing assertion of each of the first 11 was read; the\n    27\t  12th is the malformed-row ordering.\n    28\t\n    29\t## The registered $0 checks\n    30\t\n    31\t| Check | Result | Record |\n    32\t|---|---|---|\n    33\t| **T1** old-2 replayed under poc-v121 | **PASS** | `poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/t1-result.json`, `t1-replay.log` |\n    34\t| **T1b** the four refused originals | **PASS** | same file |\n    35\t| **T1c** a real v12 retry | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py` |\n    36\t| **T2** every stored shape, offline | **PASS** | `t2-result.json`, `t2-offline.log` |\n    37\t| **T3** the real validator's controls | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py` |\n    38\t| **T3b** one owner of membership | **PASS** | same |\n    39\t| **T4** sizes | printed | `t2-result.json` |\n    40\t| **T5** preflight on a judge row without a format | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py`; on old-2's real archive, part A checks its 4 refused judge rows against their saved format and preflight ends `preflight done` (`preflight-old2.log`) |\n    41\t\n    42\t### T1, old-2 replayed under poc-v121\n    43\t- 1,616 judge responses went through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions: 591→596, 6955→6979, 7068→7073, 7774→7780.\n    44\t- Every request equals old-2's outside the format.\n    45\t- Every format is strict, named `judgement`, and differs from judging-v7's only in the four constraints.\n    46\t- 0 list mismatches against the ids the text shows.\n    47\t- The store equals old-2's on all 36 shared tables, apart from the named columns:\n    48\t  - timestamps: `days_completed.at`, `processing_steps.at`, `views.created_at`;\n    49\t  - the judgements' `call_id`, `request_sha256` and `config_checksum`.\n    50\t- Positive control: one judgement's `why_changed` changed in a copy is reported as different.\n    51\t\n    52\t### T1b, the four refused originals\n    53\tEach goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id the check had refused: `e88`,\n    54\t`e3955`, `v10`, `e3998`.\n    55\t\n    56\t### T1c, a real v12 retry\n    57\tThe retry carries the first request's exact format and lists, plus the note.\n    58\t\n    59\t### T2, every stored shape\n    60\t- Population: 5,415 rows; 5,408 distinct pairs; 5,389 committed; 17 refused; 2 valid uncommitted.\n    61\t- Every committed and every valid uncommitted answer validates.\n    62\t- Every refused answer fails on its bad id:\n    63\t  - e362, e3111, e393;\n    64\t  - e88, e3955, e3998, e1382, e2769, e693;\n    65\t  - theme ids in cites (`v6`, `v10`);\n    66\t  - the dependency `v14` as evidence, twice;\n    67\t  - `v5` in `cites_views`, four times.\n    68\t\n    69\t### T3, the real validator's controls\n    70\tIn all four fields, an allowed id passes and an unlisted id fails. An empty list allows only `[]`, and a correctly typed item fails\n    71\ton length.\n    72\t\n    73\t### T3b, one owner of membership\n    74\t- With a footnote in a quote, the v12 lists and the check accept the later real id.\n    75\t- v7's text parser refuses it. That narrowing is a latent defect of the frozen versions, recorded and not fixed there.\n    76\t\n    77\t### T4, sizes\n    78\t- Over the five archives the largest request has 451 evidence ids: 464 enum values with the shared enum counted once, 915 counted per\n    79\t  reference; 5,225 characters.\n    80\t- In the sealed D358 run the largest has 647 ids: 676 counted once, 1,323 per reference. 10 of 949 requests exceed the documented\n    81\t  1,000 if the provider counts per reference; none if it counts once.\n    82\t\n    83\t### Format size\n    84\t- Characters: judging-v7's format is 1,031; v12's median is 1,396–1,405 and its max 5,225.\n    85\t- Tokens, an estimate with o200k_base on the format's JSON over all 5,415 stored requests (the provider's own count arrives with the\n    86\t  paid step): v7 315; v12 median 502, p99 1,542, max 2,621.\n    87\t- At $0.10 per million input tokens, the largest request costs about $0.00023 more.\n    88\t\n    89\t## Deviations, disclosed\n    90\t\n    91\t- **T1's first run** (`poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21/`) completed the replay, but the comparison crashed: a harness defect, since\n    92\t  FTS tables have no rowid. The transport's log was lost with it.\n    93\t  - The fixed comparison on that store found three differences. Each was named only after it was seen:\n    94\t    - `views.created_at`, a wall-clock timestamp;\n    95\t    - `link_selections`, a table the current uncommitted store schema adds (D694), empty;\n    96\t    - `dependencies.kind`, a column the same schema adds, on a table empty in both.\n    97\t  - The design's named class was \"timestamps … and new empty tables\". The added column on an empty table is the same kind, but not\n    98\t    named in advance.\n    99\t  - T1 was then rerun in full into `citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/`. It saved passing T1 and T1b results (`t1-result.json`,\n   100\t    `transport-log.json`), then exited 1: its summary print failed on a list value, a harness defect. The print is fixed, and the\n   101\t    current code exits 0 on the saved results. The saved data verifies the replay without repeating it (Codex r39 checked all 1,616\n   102\t    requests, the substitutions, the new hashes and the 36 tables).\n   103\t- **The first harness's store** is left in place, marked harness-only.\n   104\t- **Preflight** first let a refused judge row with neither a readable answer nor a saved format through with exit 0 (Codex r39,\n   105\t  reproduced). The format is now checked first; T5 covers the case, and its mutant is caught.\n   106\t- **Council round 39** (`codex-r39.md`): the build matches DESIGN v3; no v7 or v8 regression was found; T1's saved evidence holds;\n   107\t  T2 and T4 reproduce. The items above are its findings, all taken.\n   108\t\n   109\t## What the $0 test cannot show (DESIGN.md §6)\n   110\t\n   111\t- Whether the provider accepts the exact format: the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and the largest request.\n   112\t- How the provider counts a referenced enum.\n   113\t- Whether the judge, constrained, cites the intended source (e3111 could become e3110 or e3112).\n   114\t- Whether forecasts move.\n   115\t\n   116\tA paid step answers these, and it is Alex's to open. Its first part would send the largest stored request and an empty-list request\n   117\tto check acceptance. Then it would re-send the 17 stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones under v12, and read the\n   118\tcited sources beside the forecasts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba scripts/preflight.py | sed -n '57,100p'; nl -ba tests/test_citation_lists.py | sed -n '115,204p'\"","aggregated_output":"    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef saved_judge_format(request_json):\n    60\t    \"\"\"The answer format a judge request was sent with (judging-v12's differs per request, D713), or None when the row has none.\"\"\"\n    61\t    try:\n    62\t        return ((json.loads(request_json or '{}').get('response_format') or {}).get('json_schema') or {}).get('schema')\n    63\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, AttributeError):\n    64\t        return None\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef part_a(archive_conn):\n    68\t    \"\"\"(answers judged, judge rows without a saved format). Judge rows are checked against the format saved with their own request;\n    69\t    extraction and matching rows against their fixed schema.\"\"\"\n    70\t    reasons, examples, judged, missing = collections.Counter(), collections.defaultdict(list), 0, []\n    71\t    rows = archive_conn.execute(\"select purpose, request_sha256, answer_json, request_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:schema:%' or request_sha256 like '%:malformed:%' or request_sha256 like '%:refused:%'\")\n    72\t    for purpose, sha, answer_json, request_json in (tuple(r) for r in rows):\n    73\t        judged += 1\n    74\t        schema = SCHEMAS.get(purpose, {})\n    75\t        if purpose == 'judge':                     # a missing format is reported whatever the answer holds, a malformed one included\n    76\t            schema = saved_judge_format(request_json)\n    77\t            if schema is None:\n    78\t                missing.append(sha)\n    79\t                reasons['judge: no saved answer format'] += 1\n    80\t                continue\n    81\t        if ':malformed:' in sha or not answer_json:\n    82\t            reasons[f'{purpose}: not JSON'] += 1\n    83\t            continue\n    84\t        for error in model.check_schema(json.loads(answer_json), schema):\n    85\t            key = f'{purpose}: {normalise_reason(error)}'\n    86\t            reasons[key] += 1\n    87\t            examples[key].append(error[:140])\n    88\t    tally('A. answers the schema refused (prompt/schema disagreements; empty when the provider enforces the schema server-side)', judged, judged, reasons, examples)\n    89\t    return judged, missing\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tclass Unverifiable(Exception):\n    93\t    \"\"\"A stored request of a retired version, or whose configuration file is gone: counted and named in the output, not replayed,\n    94\t    and not a failure of the archive.\"\"\"\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tdef _preflight_extract_inputs(request, item, cfg):\n    98\t    \"\"\"Validate the stored source and recover exactly the question ids production showed (its [Open questions] block).\"\"\"\n    99\t    setting = cfg.extraction_setting(item['category'])\n   100\t    version = setting.prompt_version.rpartition('-')[2]\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\tdef test_an_answer_outside_the_lists_is_refused_by_the_format_before_the_check(tmp_path):\n   118\t    \"\"\"DESIGN §4.1: a membership error the provider should never return under strict mode is refused by `model.check_schema`\n   119\t    (a `:schema:` row and SchemaError), not by the check's retry.\"\"\"\n   120\t    conn = fixtures.ledger(tmp_path)\n   121\t    archive = model.Archive(str(tmp_path / 'archive.sqlite'))\n   122\t    with pytest.raises(model.SchemaError, match='e362'):\n   123\t        judging.round_of_judgements(archive, V121, conn, ['v1'], 3, DAY, transport=lambda provider, request: answer('v1', cites=['e362']))\n   124\t    assert archive.conn.execute(\"select count(*) from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:schema:%'\").fetchone()[0] == 1\n   125\t    assert store.current_state(conn, 'v1') is None\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef test_preflight_fails_on_a_refused_judge_row_without_its_saved_format(tmp_path, capsys):\n   129\t    \"\"\"T5: judge rows are checked against the format saved with their request; one without a format is named and fails preflight.\"\"\"\n   130\t    import preflight\n   131\t    archive = model.Archive(str(tmp_path / 'archive.sqlite'))\n   132\t    closed = judging.schema_for('judging-v12', {'evidence': ['e1'], 'dependencies': [], 'themes': []})\n   133\t    rows = [('judge', 'a' * 64 + ':refused:1', {'response_format': {'json_schema': {'name': 'judgement', 'strict': True, 'schema': closed}}},\n   134\t             json.loads(answer('v1', cites=['e9'])['choices'][0]['message']['content'])),\n   135\t            ('judge', 'b' * 64 + ':refused:2', {'messages': []}, json.loads(answer('v1')['choices'][0]['message']['content'])),\n   136\t            ('judge', 'd' * 64 + ':malformed:4', {'messages': []}, None)]        # no format and no readable answer (Codex r39)\n   137\t    for purpose, sha, request, data in rows:\n   138\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version='poc-v121', config_checksum='x', model='gpt-6-luna', request_sha256=sha,\n   139\t                       request_json=json.dumps(request), response_json='{}', answer_json=None if data is None else json.dumps(data), prompt_chars=1,\n   140\t                       input_tokens=1, output_tokens=1, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=0.1, created_at='2026-11-21T20:00:00')\n   141\t    archive.conn.row_factory = None\n   142\t    judged, missing = preflight.part_a(archive.conn)\n   143\t    out = capsys.readouterr().out\n   144\t    assert judged == 3 and missing == ['b' * 64 + ':refused:2', 'd' * 64 + ':malformed:4']\n   145\t    assert \"'e9' not in\" in out and 'judge: no saved answer format' in out\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\tdef test_preflights_entry_point_exits_non_zero_on_a_judge_row_without_its_saved_format(tmp_path, monkeypatch, capsys):\n   149\t    \"\"\"T5, as the user runs it: `main` finishes the other parts, then exits 1 naming the judge row part A could not check.\"\"\"\n   150\t    import preflight\n   151\t    archive = model.Archive(str(tmp_path / 'archive.sqlite'))\n   152\t    archive.record(purpose='judge', config_version='poc-v121', config_checksum='x', model='gpt-6-luna', request_sha256='c' * 64 + ':refused:3',\n   153\t                   request_json=json.dumps({'messages': []}), response_json='{}',\n   154\t                   answer_json=answer('v1')['choices'][0]['message']['content'], prompt_chars=1, input_tokens=1, output_tokens=1,\n   155\t                   cost_usd=0.0, seconds=0.1, created_at='2026-11-21T20:00:00')\n   156\t    for name in ('part_b', 'part_d'):\n   157\t        monkeypatch.setattr(preflight, name, lambda *arguments: 1)\n   158\t    monkeypatch.setattr(preflight, 'part_c', lambda *arguments: 1)\n   159\t    monkeypatch.setattr(preflight, 'part_e', lambda *arguments: None)\n   160\t    monkeypatch.setattr(preflight, 'store_copies', lambda paths: [])\n   161\t    monkeypatch.setattr(sys, 'argv', ['preflight.py', '--archive', str(tmp_path / 'archive.sqlite'), '--items', str(tmp_path / 'items.sqlite'),\n   162\t                                      '--views', str(tmp_path / 'views.sqlite')])\n   163\t    with pytest.raises(SystemExit) as stopped:\n   164\t        preflight.main()\n   165\t    assert stopped.value.code == 1 and 'FAILED: 1 refused judge rows carry no saved answer format' in capsys.readouterr().out\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 43 '\"'^## D714'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/t1_replay.py | tail -n 33\"","aggregated_output":"10721:## D714 · 2026-11-21 · judging-v12 and poc-v121 built; every registered $0 check passes; the paid acceptance step is Alex's\n10722-\n10723-- **Built (uncommitted):**\n10724-  - `judging.py`: v12, its closed format, `request_parts`, `check_answer`'s lists, and the round's per-view format;\n10725-  - `model.check_schema`: `maxItems`;\n10726-  - `prompts/judging-v12.txt`: a v7 copy;\n10727-  - `poc/config/poc-v121.json`;\n10728-  - preflight: part A on saved judge formats, and an exit on a missing one;\n10729-  - tests: `tests/test_citation_lists.py` (7) and the frozen pins.\n10730-- **Checks:** suite 388 passed; mutants 12 of 12 caught.\n10731-- **The $0 test** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md`):\n10732-  - **T1:** old-2 replayed under poc-v121. 1,616 judge responses, 4 labelled substitutions, 0 request or list problems; the store\n10733-    equals old-2's on all 36 shared tables, apart from the named columns.\n10734-  - **T1b:** the four refused originals raise `SchemaError` on their bad ids.\n10735-  - **T1c, T3, T3b, T5:** pass.\n10736-  - **T2:** 5,408 distinct pairs; all 5,391 valid answers pass; all 17 refused fail on their bad id (e362, e3111 among them).\n10737-  - **T4:** the largest request in the five archives is 464 enum values counted once (915 per reference); in the sealed D358 run, 676\n10738-    (1,323 per reference).\n10739-  - **Format tokens** (an o200k_base estimate): v7 315; v12 median 502, max 2,621.\n10740-- **Deviations, disclosed in RESULT.md:**\n10741-  - T1's first comparison crashed (FTS tables have no rowid). Three differences were named only after they were seen: a timestamp, an\n10742-    empty new table, a new column on an empty table. T1 was rerun in full.\n10743-  - Run 2's summary print failed after its passing results were saved; the print is fixed.\n10744-  - Preflight's malformed-row ordering was found by council round 39 and fixed, with a mutant.\n10745-  - A mistaken `t1_replay.py --help` started a stray replay into `./--help`. It was stopped, the folder was moved to the session\n10746-    scratchpad, and the script now refuses an option as its folder.\n10747-- **Council round 39** (`codex-r39.md`): the build matches DESIGN v3, no v7/v8 regression; its findings taken.\n10748-- **Not shown** (DESIGN §6):\n10749-  - provider acceptance of the format and its counting of a referenced enum;\n10750-  - whether the judge, constrained, cites the intended source;\n10751-  - whether forecasts move.\n10752-\n10753-  A paid step answers these, and it is Alex's (D712): acceptance on the largest and an empty-list request, then the 17 refused\n10754-  requests and a matched set of accepted ones under v12, read beside their sources.\n   235\t    cfg = config.load(str(V121))\n   236\t    out = {}\n   237\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as scratch:\n   238\t        archive = model.Archive(str(Path(scratch) / 'archive.sqlite'))\n   239\t        for call_id, item in originals.items():\n   240\t            request = item['request']\n   241\t            system, user = request['messages'][0]['content'], request['messages'][1]['content']\n   242\t            schema = request['response_format']['json_schema']['schema']\n   243\t            try:\n   244\t                model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user, schema, 'judgement', 'judge',\n   245\t                           transport=lambda provider, sent, answer=item['answer']: {'choices': [{'message': {'content': answer}}], 'usage': {}})\n   246\t                out[call_id] = 'NOT REFUSED'\n   247\t            except model.SchemaError as error:\n   248\t                out[call_id] = f'SchemaError: {str(error)[:200]}'\n   249\t    return out, all(v.startswith('SchemaError') for v in out.values()) and len(out) == EXPECTED_SUBSTITUTIONS\n   250\t\n   251\t\n   252\tdef main():\n   253\t    if len(sys.argv) != 2 or sys.argv[1].startswith('-'):\n   254\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)                  # the one argument is a new output folder, never an option\n   255\t    folder = Path(sys.argv[1])\n   256\t    result, originals = t1(folder)\n   257\t    result['T1b'], result['T1b pass'] = t1b(originals) if originals else ({}, False)\n   258\t    (folder / 't1-result.json').write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   259\t    summary = {k: v for k, v in result.items() if k not in ('store comparison',)}\n   260\t    print(json.dumps(summary, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)[:6000])\n   261\t    print(json.dumps({k: ({kk: vv for kk, vv in v.items() if kk != 'columns not compared'} if isinstance(v, dict) else v)\n   262\t                      for k, v in result['store comparison'].items()}, indent=0)[:4000])\n   263\t    sys.exit(0 if result['T1 pass'] and result['T1b pass'] else 1)\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   267\t    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
